the same day the shell does.\n\nServer (packages/cli/src/commands/reviewGit.ts, new):\n- GET /api/branches - local branches with the checked-out one marked,\n  tip subject, and git's own ahead/behind against the upstream.\n  refs/heads/ ONLY, so DESKTOP.md §1's design note (our metadata refs\n  must never appear as branches) holds structurally, not by filtering.\n- GET /api/diff/:sha?context - one commit's per-file diff parsed into\n  hunks and numbered lines, with rename/copy/binary/mode detection.\n- GET /api/overview?rev= plus `git for-ai report --rev` (the same walk\n  was missing on the CLI too). ReportData.range gains `rev`.\n- /api/meta gains `capabilities` {mode, branches, diff, actions} so one\n  SPA build serves browser and desktop by asking the server what it\n  offers instead of sniffing the client. The desktop shell now starts\n  its server with mode:\"desktop\"; `actions` is false everywhere until\n  the token-gated write endpoints exist.\n\nJudgment calls, all recorded in the file headers:\n- A merge commit is diffed against its FIRST PARENT and says so in a\n  warning. `git show` on a merge prints nothing, which would render as\n  \"this merge changed nothing\" - a lie of omission in a tool whose\n  product is honesty.\n- Truncation clips bodies, never counts: past the render budget the\n  +/- tallies keep incrementing while lines stop being stored, and\n  every clip sets a flag the UI renders.\n- An unresolvable ?rev= is a 400 with the reason, never a silently\n  empty timeline (report's unborn-HEAD leniency stays default-rev only,\n  matching log.ts).\n- Reads stay reads: plain git only, no identity minting, so the\n  byte-identical-refs guarantee still holds - the review test's\n  non-minting sweep now covers both new endpoints.\n\nUI (packages/review-ui):\n- Branch chips under the masthead scope the timeline; selection lives\n  in the URL (#/?rev=<branch>) so a branch view is reloadable.\n  DEVIATION from DESKTOP.md §3, recorded rather than done silently: the\n  plan said \"sidebar\", and this single narrow reading column would\n  spend its scarcest resource on a control used once a session. The\n  contract (a rev in, a rev out) is sidebar-ready.\n- G2 surfaced, not hidden: selecting a branch states that `ask` still\n  answers from the revision the index was built at.\n- Diff pane under the change's intent - the evidence a ledger entry\n  cannot fake. Files foldable, big commits start folded, binary /\n  rename / truncation labeled. Syntax highlighting DEFERRED (no\n  bundled highlighter earns its weight yet); recorded, not dropped.\n- Both panes gated on the capability flags, never on host sniffing.\n\nTests: 632 green (cli 233 incl. 14 new real-git ones covering root /\nrename / delete / binary / merge / truncation / detached HEAD / real\nupstream ahead-behind; review-ui 58 incl. the new pure label helpers -\nthis package has no render harness, so every label decision that could\nquietly become dishonest lives in lib/ and is tested there). Verified\nlive against this repo's own history in the browser: real branch bar,\nreal diff, and the truncation warning firing on a genuinely large\ncommit. Docs: REVIEW_UI.md §3 amended as §4 of DESKTOP.md requires,\nplus DESKTOP.md build order, ROADMAP, README.\n\nNext in DESKTOP.md: step 4b, the token-gated action endpoints and the\nactions panel.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG"},"end":"2026-07-24T23:51:54.371Z","kind":"gen_ai.tool.execution","name":"Bash","span_id":"s168","start":"2026-07-24T23:51:54.371Z"}],"summary":"claude-code session: 156 tool execution(s), 12 model turn(s) for commit \"Branches and diffs: the desktop app's step 2+3, shipped to the browser too\"."}